        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>10. Creators and Third-Party Content</h2>
            
            <h3>10.1 Becoming a Creator</h3>
            <p>
                Users may apply to become creators on Streamtunes. Creators may upload their original music to the platform for streaming. To become a creator, you must:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Successfully onboard with Streamtunes, its designated tax service, and its designated payment processor so that we can pay you stream-based earnings for streams of the music you upload to the Service</li>
                <li>Provide accurate, complete, and current information during onboarding, including required tax documentation</li>
                <li>Have original music that you own or have sufficient legal rights to distribute</li>
                <li>Comply with all applicable local, national, and international laws and regulations related to music distribution and monetization</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>10.2 Creator Responsibilities</h3>
            <p>
                As a creator on Streamtunes, you are solely responsible for:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Ensuring you hold all necessary copyrights, licenses, and permissions to upload and distribute your music</li>
                <li>Resolving any disputes, claims, or legal issues arising from your music or creator activities</li>
                <li>Ensuring your content does not infringe or violate the rights of any third party</li>
                <li>Complying with all applicable tax, reporting, and regulatory obligations</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>10.3 Stream-Based Earnings and Payments</h3>
            <p>
                Creators may earn stream-based earnings from streams of their music on the platform under the following structure:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Pay Rate:</strong> Creators are paid per stream at a rate established at the time of creator onboarding (typically $@_streamPayRateDisplay.ToString("F2") per 1,000 streams, or $@_streamPayRatePerStream.ToString("F3") per stream). This rate is locked in for the lifetime of the creator account unless modified by written agreement or required by law.</li>
                <li><strong>Stream Definition:</strong> A stream is counted when a user plays a song for at least @_streamQualifyingSeconds continuous seconds without seeking or looping.</li>
                <li><strong>Payout Schedule:</strong> Stream-based earnings are processed weekly, every Monday at 1:00 AM UTC, subject to payment processor availability and compliance checks.</li>
                <li><strong>Minimum Payout:</strong> Creators must accrue at least $5.00 in unpaid stream-based earnings to receive a payout.</li>
                <li><strong>Payment Frequency:</strong> Creators may receive no more than one payout per week.</li>
                <li><strong>Payment Method:</strong> All payouts are issued through Streamtunes' designated payment processor. Streamtunes does not custody creator funds.</li>
                <li><strong>Receipts:</strong> Creators will receive an electronic, itemized payout receipt detailing stream counts and earnings, subject to payment processor availability and compliance checks, and as long as there are no technical issues.</li>
                <li><strong>Example:</strong> If a creator accrues 1,000 total qualifying streams at $@_streamPayRatePerStream.ToString("F3") per stream, the creator earns $@_streamPayRateDisplay.ToString("F2") and will be paid on the next eligible payout date.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>10.4 No Guaranteed Earnings</h3>
            <p>
                Creators acknowledge that stream-based earnings are not guaranteed. Earnings depend on factors including, but not limited to, user activity, listener behavior, availability of the Service, compliance with these Terms, and platform policies. Streamtunes makes no guarantees regarding minimum streams, earnings, exposure, promotion, or revenue.
            </p>

            <h3>10.5 Creator Eligibility and Service Location (Platform Policy)</h3>
            <p>
                Streamtunes supports <strong>paid creator participation</strong> only if:
            </p>
            <ol>
                <li>You are a <strong>U.S. person</strong> for U.S. tax purposes; or</li>
                <li>You are <strong>not a U.S. person</strong> and you will perform <strong>all creator activities for Streamtunes entirely outside the United States</strong>.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>
                Creators who are not U.S. persons and who will perform any creator activities while physically present in the United States are <strong>not eligible to receive payouts</strong> through the Service at this time.
            </p>
            <p>
                For purposes of this section, <strong>creator activities</strong> include uploading content, managing or modifying uploaded content, maintaining a creator account, and any other actions related to monetized participation on the Service.
            </p>

            <h3>10.6 Taxes and Reporting</h3>
            <p>
                Creators acknowledge and agree that they are solely responsible for determining, reporting, and paying all applicable taxes arising from payments received through the Service, including but not limited to income taxes, self-employment taxes, VAT, GST, sales taxes, or similar obligations.
